{"title":"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 39","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_39&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The length of service a chair cover will give varies directly as the strength of the fabric and inversely as the amount of wear it receives. If one fabric, which is twice as strong as a second fabric and receives three times as much wear, lasts for 4 years, how long will the second fabric last?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e4183a920460797b8e749c548b8215977677a98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\quad 9; \\quad \\text{(B)} \\quad 4; \\quad \\text{(C)} \\quad 2; \\quad \\text{(D)} \\quad 6; \\quad \\text{(E)} \\quad \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"438\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_39&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's call how long a chair cover lasts (or its length of service) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />. If the strength of the fabric is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and the amount of wear it receives is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45a59d0c656a002b397155df79afde22fde2246.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\ell \\propto \\frac{s}{w},\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"32\" />\n(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/11303cd923877716bbb6fde144d09687260910fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\propto$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"9\" /> is the symbol for proportional to)\n</p><p>or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/094c27e5a9310ac0b65bcf9a31e010d875e0916f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell = \\left(\\frac{s}{w}\\right)k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"83\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is some number.\n</p><p>For the second fabric, it gets 3 times as much wear, lasts four years and is twice as strong, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2fece347a3f154fb937bfc4e166aa597e18cc1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 = \\left(\\frac{2s}{3w}\\right)k.\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now, if we solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4fd05e28223281bc566e0b6eb4e5701483369c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{w}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"33\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb1ed396f2d3a3d6d6e4915ce41695d84acf5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{w}=\\frac{6}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>If we plug this value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4fd05e28223281bc566e0b6eb4e5701483369c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{w}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"33\" /> back into our original equation (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e7d535795d994fa091d36d555653e5a8a57b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell=\\left(\\frac{s}{w}\\right)k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"83\" height=\"33\" />), the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />'s cancel out:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db8763205843e56bb332da4a3c0fb44ebab44af0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\ell = \\left(\\frac{s}{w}\\right)k=\\left(\\frac{6}{k}\\right)k=6.\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc93afd012d6af697c4fae71d14de49f021d78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />, 6 years.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_39&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Imagine a third fabric with half the strength of the second one. This will last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b5303e617471e7ac98c4549eed97c20d4ed0a91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{2}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> years since strength is directly proportional to the time.\n</p><p>This third fabric receives three times more wear than the first. This means that the first fabric will last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af21061ddcd2ade9d859dd59a4dd7ed25a091ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{1/3}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"66\" height=\"43\" /> years. (The wear is inversely proportional to the time.)\n</p><p>This gives that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc93afd012d6af697c4fae71d14de49f021d78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_39&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contests\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests\">1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a>)</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_38\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 38\"> Problem 38</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"40%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_Past_Problems/Solutions\" title=\"TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions\">TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_40\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 40\"> Problem 40</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041658\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 127/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 664/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 308/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3624/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.272      1 Template:Succession_box\n100.00%    7.272      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20682:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041658 and revision id 144662. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}